[gd_scene load_steps=11 format=3]

; The Voice Recognition Unit (NUS-020): the grey dongle that hangs off a cord
; ending in an ordinary N64 controller plug, with the NUS-021 microphone plugged
; into a 3.5 mm jack on its front.
;
; It does NOT sit in a controller socket itself -- it used to, and its front end
; was moulded as a connector tongue to suit. The plug on its cord does that now,
; the same generic moulding every other controller wears, so this shell is just a
; shell: a slab with a crown that rises toward the back, the jack in the front
; face at -Z, and the cord to the console leaving the back at +Z. The origin is
; the middle of the base's underside, so it sits where it is put.
;
; No sticker and no logo: this is our own shell, not a copy of a printed one.
;
; Every part is sunk into its neighbour. Two faces at one depth facing the same
; way trade pixels -- see the header of n64_vru_cable.tscn for the flicker that
; cost, and n64_vru_tests "faces/" for the check that fails if it returns.
;
; Sizes are estimated from photographs -- no dimensioned drawing was found.

